       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum ibuprofen dose for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and the usual limit for a single dose is 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a mix-up with the daily total. Possible intended orders:\n\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inpatient anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), a common analgesic dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then add it as a note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
